---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/ui/CodeBlock.astro';

const dockerfile = `# Multi-stage Production Dockerfile for CopyPatch Server
FROM node:20-alpine AS base
WORKDIR /app
RUN npm install -g pnpm@11.10.0

# Dependencies Stage
FROM base AS deps
COPY package.json pnpm-lock.yaml pnpm-workspace.yaml ./
COPY packages/core/package.json ./packages/core/
COPY packages/server/package.json ./packages/server/
RUN pnpm install --prod --frozen-lockfile

# Runner Stage
FROM node:20-alpine AS runner
WORKDIR /app

ENV NODE_ENV=production
ENV PORT=4040
ENV DB_PATH=/data/copypatch.sqlite

# Create persistent storage volume mount
RUN mkdir -p /data && chown -R node:node /data
VOLUME /data

COPY --from=deps --chown=node:node /app/node_modules ./node_modules
COPY --from=deps --chown=node:node /app/packages/core/node_modules ./packages/core/node_modules
COPY --from=deps --chown=node:node /app/packages/server/node_modules ./packages/server/node_modules
COPY --chown=node:node packages/core/dist ./packages/core/dist
COPY --chown=node:node packages/server/dist ./packages/server/dist
COPY --chown=node:node package.json pnpm-workspace.yaml ./
COPY --chown=node:node packages/core/package.json ./packages/core/
COPY --chown=node:node packages/server/package.json ./packages/server/

USER node
EXPOSE 4040

HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=5s --start-period=5s --retries=3 \
  CMD wget --no-verbose --tries=1 --spider http://localhost:4040/health || exit 1

CMD ["node", "packages/server/dist/cli/bin.js", "serve", "--port", "4040", "--db", "/data/copypatch.sqlite", "--origin", "https://yourdomain.com"]`;

const dockerCompose = `version: "3.8"

services:
  copypatch:
    image: copypatch-server:latest
    build:
      context: .
      dockerfile: Dockerfile
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "127.0.0.1:4040:4040"
    environment:
      - NODE_ENV=production
      - PORT=4040
      - DB_PATH=/data/copypatch.sqlite
      - ORIGIN=https://my-website.com
      - MODE=direct
    volumes:
      - copypatch_data:/data
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD", "wget", "-qO-", "http://localhost:4040/health"]
      interval: 30s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 3

volumes:
  copypatch_data:
    driver: local`;

const systemdUnit = `[Unit]
Description=CopyPatch Standalone Server
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=simple
User=copypatch
Group=copypatch
WorkingDirectory=/var/www/copypatch
ExecStart=/usr/bin/node packages/server/dist/cli/bin.js serve --port 4040 --db /var/lib/copypatch/copypatch.sqlite --origin https://my-website.com
Restart=always
RestartSec=10
Environment=NODE_ENV=production

# Security Sandbox Directives
NoNewPrivileges=true
ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=true
ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/copypatch
PrivateTmp=true

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target`;

const caddyfile = `my-website.com {
    encode gzip zstd

    # Route CopyPatch API endpoints directly to backend server
    handle /__copypatch/api/v1/* {
        reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:4040 {
            header_up Host {host}
            header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
            header_up X-Forwarded-Proto {scheme}
        }
    }

    # Public static frontend or Next.js server
    handle {
        reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3000
    }
}`;

const flyConfig = `app = "my-copypatch-server"
primary_region = "fra"

[mounts]
  source = "copypatch_data"
  destination = "/data"

[http_service]
  internal_port = 4040
  force_https = true
  auto_stop_machines = false
  auto_start_machines = true
  min_machines_running = 1

[[vm]]
  size = "shared-cpu-1x"
  memory = "256mb"`;

const litestreamConfig = `dbs:
  - path: /data/copypatch.sqlite
    replicas:
      - type: s3
        bucket: my-copypatch-backups
        path: production/copypatch.sqlite
        endpoint: s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com
        access-key-id: \${AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID}
        secret-access-key: \${AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY}
        retention: 720h`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Deployment Guide"
  description="Production self-hosting recipes for CopyPatch with Docker, systemd, Caddy, Nginx, Fly.io, Railway, and Litestream."
>
  <h1>Self-Hosted Deployment Guide</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    CopyPatch is designed for effortless, deterministic self-hosting. Because persistence lives in a single SQLite database in Write-Ahead Logging (WAL) mode with zero external service dependencies, a standard single-node server handles millions of monthly requests for under $5/month.
  </p>

  <h2>Deployment Strategies</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Method</th>
        <th>Best For</th>
        <th>Persistence Mechanism</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Docker & Compose</strong></td>
        <td>Containerized infrastructure (VPS, Coolify, Portainer)</td>
        <td>Mounted Volume (<code>/data</code>)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>systemd Unit</strong></td>
        <td>Bare-metal Linux / Ubuntu / Debian VM</td>
        <td>Local Directory (<code>/var/lib/copypatch</code>)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Fly.io / Railway</strong></td>
        <td>Managed Cloud Containers</td>
        <td>Attached Persistent Disk Volume</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>1. Docker Production Image</h2>
  <p>
    Use a multi-stage Docker build to keep your container slim and ensure the SQLite database directory is mounted as a persistent volume:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock code={dockerfile} lang="dockerfile" title="Dockerfile" />

  <h2>2. Docker Compose Configuration</h2>
  <p>
    Deploy CopyPatch alongside your host application behind a reverse proxy using Docker Compose:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock code={dockerCompose} lang="yaml" title="docker-compose.yml" />

  <h2>3. Native Linux systemd Service</h2>
  <p>
    For dedicated Linux virtual machines (DigitalOcean, Hetzner, AWS EC2, Linode), manage the process with systemd:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock code={systemdUnit} lang="ini" title="/etc/systemd/system/copypatch.service" />

  <p>
    Enable and start the service:
  </p>
  <pre><code>sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable --now copypatch</code></pre>

  <h2>4. Reverse Proxy Setup (Caddy / Nginx)</h2>
  <p>
    Serving both your frontend app and CopyPatch under the same origin (or cleanly routing <code>/__copypatch/api/v1</code>) ensures cookies, CSRF tokens, and SameSite validation operate seamlessly without cross-origin friction.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock code={caddyfile} lang="nginx" title="Caddyfile" />

  <h2>5. Fly.io Deployment with Persistent Storage</h2>
  <p>
    Create a Fly.io persistent volume and deploy with <code>fly.toml</code>:
  </p>
  <pre><code>fly volumes create copypatch_data --region fra --size 1</code></pre>

  <CodeBlock code={flyConfig} lang="toml" title="fly.toml" />

  <h2>6. Continuous Backups with Litestream</h2>
  <p>
    Because CopyPatch runs SQLite in WAL mode, you can use <strong>Litestream</strong> to replicate changes to AWS S3, Cloudflare R2, or Backblaze B2 in real-time with zero read/write locks:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock code={litestreamConfig} lang="yaml" title="/etc/litestream.yml" />

  <h2>Production Checklist</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>HTTPS:</strong> Always enable TLS/HTTPS in production to enforce <code>Secure</code> and <code>SameSite=Strict</code> session cookies.</li>
    <li><strong>Passphrase Complexity:</strong> Use an editor passphrase with at least 16 random characters.</li>
    <li><strong>Allowed Origin:</strong> Set <code>--origin https://yourdomain.com</code> to restrict write access exclusively to your legitimate domain.</li>
    <li><strong>Disk Mounting:</strong> Verify that <code>copypatch.sqlite</code>, <code>copypatch.sqlite-wal</code>, and <code>copypatch.sqlite-shm</code> reside on persistent storage.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
